When the user requests implementation of a new feature related to TradingView Charting Library:
1. Automatically consult doc_links.md to identify the most relevant documentation links
2. Suggest these specific documentation resources to the user
3. Offer to visit these links and summarize the relevant implementation details
4. Only apply this behavior for TradingView Charting Library feature requests, not for general programming questions
5. Provide implementation guidance based on the documentation when appropriate
6. Reference relevant example files in the codebase, specifically:
   - HTML examples: /public/index.html, /public/themed.html, /public/mobile_black.html, /public/mobile_white.html, /public/test.html
   - Library type definitions: /public/charting_library.d.ts, /public/charting_library/charting_library.d.ts, /public/charting_library/datafeed-api.d.ts
   - Datafeed implementations: /public/datafeeds/ directory
   - Library implementations: /public/charting_library/charting_library.js and its variants (.esm.js, .cjs.js, .standalone.js)
7. When resolving implementation issues, check both the official documentation and the example implementations in the codebase
8. For complex integrations, refer to actual implementation in the codebase before suggesting new approaches
